"Ihr habt Ivan den Klugen geschlagen.  Kehrt mit der Siegesurkunde zu Jarl Markel von Guberland zurück."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/english/quests_overlay.txt:8
msgid ""
"Find a way off the island.\n"
"\n"
"There's got to be some way off this rock.  Maybe there are a few inhabitants that could help you."
msgstr ""
"Findet einen Weg, die Insel zu verlassen.\n"
"\n"
"Es muß doch einen Weg von diesem Felsen geben.  Vielleicht gibt es hier ein paar Bewohner, die Euch helfen könnten."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/english/quests_overlay.txt:80
msgid ""
"Retrieve Thjorad from Lindisfarne.\n"
"\n"
"Go to the Lindisfarne Monastery in Lindisfarne and retrieve the artifact called Thjorad.  Return it to Jarl Sven of Thjorgard."
msgstr ""
"Holt Thjorad aus Lindisfarne.\n"
"\n"
"Geht zum Kloster Lindisfarne in Lindisfarne und holt das Artefakt namens Thjorad.  Bringt es zu Jarl Sven von Thjorgard."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/english/quests_overlay.txt:83
msgid ""
"Retrieve Thjorad from Lindisfarne.\n"
"\n"
"You've got Thjorad.  Now return it to Jarl Sven of Thjorgard."
msgstr ""
"Holt Thjorad aus Lindisfarne.\n"
"\n"
"Ihr habt Thjorad.  Bringt es nun zu Jarl Sven von Thjorgard."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/english/quests_overlay.txt:86
msgid ""
"Find out why the Elemental Thjorad production has stopped.\n"
"\n"
"Go to the Thjorad Mine in Thjorgard and find out why they have stopped producing Elemental Thjorad.  Return to Jarl Sven of Thjorgard when they are once again producing Elemental Thjorad."
msgstr ""
"Findet heraus, warum die Förderung von Elementar-Thjorad zum Erliegen gekommen ist.\n"
"\n"
"Geht zur Thjorad-Mine in Thjorgard und findet heraus, warum dort kein Elementar-Thjorad mehr gefördert wird.  Kehrt zu Jarl Sven von Thjorgard zurück, wenn wieder Elementar-Thjorad gefördert wird."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/english/quests_overlay.txt:89
msgid ""
"Find the cave-in\n"
"\n"
"A section of the mine is about to cave in.  Find it and see if there is anything you can do about it."
msgstr ""
"Findet die Einsturzstelle\n"
"\n"
"Ein Teil der Mine droht einzustürzen.  Findet ihn und seht nach, ob Ihr etwas dagegen tun könnt."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/english/quests_overlay.txt:92
msgid ""
"Break through the hard rock.\n"
"\n"
"There is a section of rock that is too tough for the miner's picks.  Find it and try to break through it."
msgstr ""
"Durchbrecht den harten Fels.\n"
"\n"
"Es gibt einen Felsabschnitt, der für die Spitzhacken der Bergleute zu hart ist.  Findet ihn und versucht, ihn zu durchbrechen."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/english/quests_overlay.txt:95
msgid ""
"Fix the refinery machine.\n"
"\n"
"The slag extractor is broken.  Find Hjarrand the Fixer in Thjorgard.  He should remember how to fix the machine."
msgstr ""
"Repariert die Maschine der Raffinerie.\n"
"\n"
"Der Schlackenabscheider ist kaputt.  Findet Hjarrand Flickmann in Thjorgard.  Er sollte sich noch erinnern, wie man die Maschine repariert."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/english/quests_overlay.txt:98
msgid ""
"Fix the refinery machine.\n"
"\n"
"You've paid Hjarrand to look at the Machine.  Meet him at the Mine."
msgstr ""
"Repariert die Maschine der Raffinerie.\n"
"\n"
"Ihr habt Hjarrand bezahlt, damit er sich die Maschine ansieht.  Trefft ihn bei der Mine."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/hirelings.txt:2 assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/hirelings.txt:3 assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/hirelings.txt:5
msgid "Arrow"
msgstr "Pfeil"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:10
msgid "Flamberge"
msgstr "Flamberge"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:10
msgid ""
"This was the type of sword used by the bastard son of the Ursanian Emperor during the earthquakes that tore the Empire apart and the Revolution that followed.  It's wavy blade was thought to cause more damage."
msgstr ""
"Diese Art Schwert benutzte der Bastardsohn des Ursanischen Kaisers während der Erdbeben, die das Reich zerrissen, und der darauf folgenden Revolution.  Man glaubte, daß seine gewellte Klinge größeren Schaden anrichtet."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:100
msgid ""
"These boots are made from steel, with leather inside to increase comfort."
msgstr ""
"Diese Stiefel sind aus Stahl gefertigt und innen mit Leder ausgekleidet, damit sie bequemer sind."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:101
msgid "Sabaton"
msgstr "Sabaton"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:101
msgid ""
"These are steel boots made to be worn with a suit of Plate armor. They are made of steel, have leather insoles, and mail to cover the ankle joint."
msgstr ""
"Dies sind Stahlstiefel, die zu einer Plattenrüstung getragen werden. Sie sind aus Stahl gefertigt, haben Ledersohlen und Kettengeflecht, das das Fußgelenk bedeckt."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:102
msgid ""
"Old Ursanian for \"Protector of Feet\", the making of these shoes has been lost to history. They are strong, have virtually no break-in period, and have magicial wardings in them to stop your heel from being disconnected from your ankle."
msgstr ""
"Altursanisch für \"Beschützer der Füße\"; die Kunst, diese Schuhe herzustellen, ist in der Geschichte verlorengegangen. Sie sind robust, müssen so gut wie gar nicht eingelaufen werden und enthalten magische Schutzzauber, die verhindern, daß sich Eure Ferse von Eurem Knöchel löst."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:102
msgid "Prote der Fatta"
msgstr "Prote der Fatta"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:103 assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:104 assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:105
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:106 assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:107 assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:108
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:109 assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:110 assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:111
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:165 assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:186 assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:196
msgid "Gloves"
msgstr "Handschuhe"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:103
msgid ""
"These gloves are more often seen at the Thing than in combat. Nonetheless, they offer better protection than a bare hand."
msgstr ""
"Diese Handschuhe sieht man öfter beim Thing als im Kampf. Dennoch bieten sie mehr Schutz als eine bloße Hand."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:104
msgid "Leather Gauntlets"
msgstr "Lederpanzerhandschuhe"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:104
msgid ""
"These hardened leather gauntlets have articulated fingers, and a softer leather palm for better feel of the weapon"
msgstr ""
"Diese Panzerhandschuhe aus gehärtetem Leder haben bewegliche Finger und eine weichere Lederinnenfläche, damit man die Waffe besser spürt"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:105
msgid "Mail Gauntlets"
msgstr "Kettenhandschuhe"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:105
msgid ""
"These gloves have a leather palm, and are backed with mail. They don't quite fit properly, but are effective for stopping glancing blows from doing serious damage."
msgstr ""
"Diese Handschuhe haben eine Lederinnenfläche und einen mit Kettengeflecht besetzten Handrücken. Sie passen nicht ganz richtig, verhindern aber wirksam, daß Streifschläge ernsthaften Schaden anrichten."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:106
msgid ""
"These steel gauntlets are the first major step in protecting the hand. They are a major step up from mail gauntlets, offering more protection, while not sacrificing much flexibility."
msgstr ""
"Diese Stahlhandschuhe sind der erste große Schritt zum Schutz der Hand. Sie sind den Kettenhandschuhen weit überlegen und bieten mehr Schutz, ohne viel Beweglichkeit einzubüßen."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:107
msgid "Exceptional Mail Gauntlets"
msgstr "Außergewöhnliche Kettenhandschuhe"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:107
msgid ""
"These mail gauntlets are made of a resilient alloy whose secret is only known to the mailsmiths. It's flexibility and strength makes this gauntlet offer great protection."
msgstr ""
"Diese Kettenhandschuhe bestehen aus einer widerstandsfähigen Legierung, deren Geheimnis nur die Kettenschmiede kennen. Dank ihrer Beweglichkeit und Stärke bieten diese Handschuhe großen Schutz."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:108
msgid "Superior Steel Gauntlets"
msgstr "Erlesene Stahlhandschuhe"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:108
msgid ""
"These gauntlets are made from the finest steel available. Each finger is seperately articulated, and the rivits holding them in place are of the highest quality. You would he hard pressed to find better armor for the hand than this."
msgstr ""
"Diese Panzerhandschuhe sind aus dem feinsten Stahl gefertigt, den es gibt. Jeder Finger ist einzeln beweglich, und die Nieten, die sie zusammenhalten, sind von höchster Qualität. Einen besseren Schutz für die Hand werdet Ihr kaum finden."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:109
msgid ""
"Old Ursanian for \"Protector of Hands\"  These gloves are copied from pictures in tapestries and plates from centuries ago. They offer a great deal of protection, but it is certain, as many scholars attest, these copies are no match for the originals."
msgstr ""
"Altursanisch für \"Beschützer der Hände\".  Diese Handschuhe wurden nach Abbildungen auf jahrhundertealten Wandteppichen und Tellern nachgebildet. Sie bieten großen Schutz, doch wie viele Gelehrte bezeugen, können es diese Nachbildungen gewiß nicht mit den Originalen aufnehmen."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:109
msgid "Prote der Hanne"
msgstr "Prote der Hanne"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:11
msgid "The Chopper"
msgstr "Der Hacker"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:11
msgid ""
"The Chopper was originally a ritual sword until it was discovered it had surprising military value."
msgstr ""
"Der Hacker war ursprünglich ein Ritualschwert, bis man entdeckte, daß er einen überraschenden militärischen Wert besaß."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:110
msgid "Processional Gauntlets"
msgstr "Prozessionshandschuhe"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:110
msgid ""
"These gauntlets are used more for parades and Stately matters than for fighting. Yet they were designed for combat. They are comfortable, sharp looking, and keep your hands safe."
msgstr ""
"Diese Panzerhandschuhe werden eher bei Paraden und Staatsangelegenheiten getragen als im Kampf. Dennoch wurden sie für den Kampf entworfen. Sie sind bequem, sehen schneidig aus und schützen Eure Hände."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:111
msgid "Magreeb Gauntlets"
msgstr "Magreeb-Panzerhandschuhe"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:111
msgid ""
"These gauntlets are so named because they resemble the claw like arm of the Magreeb. Despite the fancified claws, they are still flexible and strong. The claws on them are also very sharp, and could possibly be used as a weapon themselves."
msgstr ""
"Diese Panzerhandschuhe tragen ihren Namen, weil sie dem klauenartigen Arm des Magreeb ähneln. Trotz der verzierten Klauen sind sie beweglich und stark. Die Klauen sind zudem sehr scharf und könnten womöglich selbst als Waffe dienen."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:112
msgid "Footman's Buckler"
msgstr "Buckler des Fußsoldaten"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:112
msgid ""
"Mass produced for the Arena, the Footman's Buckler was quickly adopted for use during the Clan Wars."
msgstr ""
"Der Buckler des Fußsoldaten wurde für die Arena in großen Mengen hergestellt und während der Clankriege rasch auch im Kampf übernommen."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:113
msgid ""
"This small round shield is cheap, and easy to make. It's price makes it very popular."
msgstr ""
"Dieser kleine Rundschild ist billig und leicht herzustellen. Sein Preis macht ihn sehr beliebt."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:114
msgid ""
"The favored shield of the Jarls of Chedian, the Kite shield provides better protection than the Footman's Buckler.  It is often painted with the Jarl's Bindrune."
msgstr ""
"Der Drachenschild ist der bevorzugte Schild der Jarls von Chedian und bietet besseren Schutz als der Buckler des Fußsoldaten.  Er ist oft mit der Binderune des Jarls bemalt."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:115
msgid "Heater"
msgstr "Dreieckschild"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:115
msgid ""
"This medium sized shield is a favorite of Mercenaries. It is made of wood, and reinforced with steel."
msgstr ""
"Dieser mittelgroße Schild ist bei Söldnern sehr beliebt. Er ist aus Holz gefertigt und mit Stahl verstärkt."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:116
msgid "Pavise"
msgstr "Pavese"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:116
msgid ""
"This is the shield used by crossbowmen to protect themselves while reloading their weapon"
msgstr ""
"Mit diesem Schild schützen sich Armbrustschützen, während sie ihre Waffe nachladen"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:117
msgid "Ronenguard Shield"
msgstr "Ronenguard-Schild"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:117
msgid ""
"This is the sheild used most often by the Ronenhall Guard. It is made of solid steel. It is heavier than most other sheilds, but the strong members of the Ronenhall Guard use it very well."
msgstr ""
"Dies ist der Schild, den die Ronenhall-Garde am häufigsten benutzt. Er ist aus massivem Stahl gefertigt. Er ist schwerer als die meisten anderen Schilde, doch die starken Mitglieder der Ronenhall-Garde wissen ihn sehr gut zu führen."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:118
msgid ""
"Literally, Old Ursanian for \"Soldier Protector\"  These shields were found in an abandon warehouse in the Old Ursana. They are rare, and exceptionally strong."
msgstr ""
"Wörtlich Altursanisch für \"Beschützer des Soldaten\".  Diese Schilde wurden in einem verlassenen Lagerhaus im Alten Ursana gefunden. Sie sind selten und außergewöhnlich stark."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:118
msgid "Prote der Solle"
msgstr "Prote der Solle"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:119
msgid "Haklea Shovis"
msgstr "Haklea Shovis"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:119
msgid ""
"This shield comes from a shipment of shields that washed up on Lachmon Cove from an unknown shipwreck. It's name is derived from the words written on the side of the crates. It's origins and history are not known, but it is one of the strongest and lightest shields you can carry."
msgstr ""
"Dieser Schild stammt aus einer Ladung Schilde, die von einem unbekannten Schiffswrack an der Lachmon-Bucht angespült wurde. Sein Name leitet sich von den Worten ab, die auf der Seite der Kisten standen. Seine Herkunft und Geschichte sind unbekannt, doch er ist einer der stärksten und leichtesten Schilde, die man tragen kann."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:12
msgid "Stiletto"
msgstr "Stilett"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:12
msgid "This dagger is designed for stabbing and piercing mail."
msgstr ""
"Dieser Dolch ist dafür gemacht, zuzustechen und Kettenpanzer zu durchbohren."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:120
msgid "Peasant Belt"
msgstr "Bauerngürtel"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:120
msgid "This belt is commonly seen all over Chedian."
msgstr "Diesen Gürtel sieht man überall in Chedian."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:121
msgid "Fancy Belt"
msgstr "Prunkgürtel"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:121
msgid ""
"This belt is often sold by merchants to lower classes, who often try to copy the fashion of the Jarls."
msgstr ""
"Diesen Gürtel verkaufen Händler oft an die unteren Schichten, die gern die Mode der Jarls nachahmen."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:122
msgid "Soldier's Belt"
msgstr "Soldatengürtel"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:122
msgid ""
"This is the belt most often seen worn by soldiers in Framon to hold their swords up."
msgstr ""
"Diesen Gürtel tragen die Soldaten in Framon am häufigsten, um ihre Schwerter daran zu befestigen."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:123
msgid "Regal Belt"
msgstr "Königlicher Gürtel"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:123
msgid "This belt is a symbol of nobility and is often worn to show status."
msgstr ""
"Dieser Gürtel ist ein Zeichen des Adels und wird oft getragen, um den eigenen Stand zu zeigen."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:124
msgid "Dragon Belt"
msgstr "Drachengürtel"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:124
msgid ""
"This Belt was made from the scales of a dragon. It is sturdy, and nearly unbreakable."
msgstr ""
"Dieser Gürtel wurde aus den Schuppen eines Drachen gefertigt. Er ist robust und nahezu unzerstörbar."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:125
msgid "Iron Ring"
msgstr "Eisenring"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:125
msgid "Not the most fancy of jewelry, this is a simple ring made of iron."
msgstr ""
"Kein besonders prächtiges Schmuckstück, sondern ein einfacher Ring aus Eisen."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:126
msgid "This is a small gold band, popular with the Chedian nobles."
msgstr ""
"Dies ist ein schmaler Goldreif, der bei den Adligen von Chedian beliebt ist."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:127
msgid "Puzzle Ring"
msgstr "Vexierring"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:127
msgid ""
"The initial design of the puzzle ring was made by the Archmage Jesper, who found that the twisted puzzle like ring was very susceptible to enchantment."
msgstr ""
"Der erste Vexierring wurde vom Erzmagier Jesper entworfen, der herausfand, daß sich der verschlungene, rätselhafte Ring sehr gut verzaubern ließ."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:128
msgid "A large, lovely pearl adorns this otherwise unremarkable ring."
msgstr ""
"Eine große, wunderschöne Perle schmückt diesen ansonsten unauffälligen Ring."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:129
msgid "Diamond Ring"
msgstr "Diamantring"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:129
msgid "Simple gold band with several fat diamonds mounted in it."
msgstr ""
"Ein einfacher Goldreif, in den mehrere dicke Diamanten eingefaßt sind."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:13
msgid "Elite Dagger"
msgstr "Elitedolch"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:13
msgid "Standard issue dagger of the Drangheim Prison guards."
msgstr "Der Standarddolch der Wachen im Gefängnis von Drangheim."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:130
msgid ""
"Plain Bronze Amulet, probably meant as a blank for some other design. Not worth much."
msgstr ""
"Ein schlichtes Bronzeamulett, vermutlich als Rohling für eine andere Verzierung gedacht. Nicht viel wert."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:131
msgid "Lightly decorated platinum amulet."
msgstr "Ein leicht verziertes Platinamulett."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:131
msgid "Platinum Amulet"
msgstr "Platinamulett"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:132
msgid "Gemmed Amulet"
msgstr "Juwelenamulett"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:132
msgid "Golden amulet shaped as a star, encrusted with gems."
msgstr "Ein sternförmiges, mit Edelsteinen besetztes Goldamulett."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:133
msgid ""
"This amulet was cast to resemble the face of a now-unknown Warrior-God."
msgstr ""
"Dieses Amulett wurde so gegossen, daß es dem Antlitz eines heute unbekannten Kriegergottes gleicht."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:133
msgid "Warrior Amulet"
msgstr "Kriegeramulett"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:134
msgid ""
"Made from elemental Thjorad by Thjoradric Smiths. It is of a very high quality."
msgstr ""
"Von thjoradrischen Schmieden aus Elementar-Thjorad gefertigt. Es ist von sehr hoher Qualität."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:134
msgid "Thjoradric Amulet"
msgstr "Thjoradrisches Amulett"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:135
msgid "Sing Sword"
msgstr "Singschwert"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:135
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This sword was enchanted by an unknown mage for the doctor turned skald known as Frank.  It is said to cast a pleasing tone in battle, causing the weilder to become stronger. (Effects: +30 to Might; of Arms Mastery)"
msgid ""
"This sword was enchanted by an unknown mage for the doctor turned skald known as Frank.  It is said to cast a pleasing tone in battle, causing the wielder to become stronger. (Effects: +30 Might, +5 Armsmaster)"
msgstr ""
"Dieses Schwert wurde von einem unbekannten Magier für den Arzt verzaubert, der zum Skalden wurde und als Frank bekannt ist.  Man sagt, es lasse im Kampf einen wohlklingenden Ton erklingen, der seinen Träger stärker macht. (Effekte: +30 Stärke; des Waffenmeisters)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:136
msgid "Excala Banna"
msgstr "Excala Banna"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:136
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This yellow-hued sword is legendary among the native people of Frosgard.  They claim that it was carried by their hero Eric, who it seemed was never prepared for battle.  It is supposed to have surfaced from a lake when Eric cried out, \"Yoohoo!\" (Effects: -5 Accuracy, +15 Endurance, +50 Luck)"
msgid ""
"This yellow-hued sword is legendary among the native people of Frosgard.  They claim that it was carried by their hero Eric, who it seemed was never prepared for battle.  It is supposed to have surfaced from a lake when Eric cried out, \"Yoohoo!\" (Effects: +15 Endurance, -5 Accuracy, +50 Luck)"
msgstr ""
"Dieses gelblich schimmernde Schwert ist bei den Ureinwohnern von Frosgard legendär.  Sie behaupten, es sei von ihrem Helden Eric getragen worden, der anscheinend nie auf einen Kampf vorbereitet war.  Es soll aus einem See aufgetaucht sein, als Eric \"Juhuu!\" rief. (Effekte: -5 Genauigkeit, +15 Ausdauer, +50 Glück)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:137
msgid "Mevan Sword"
msgstr "Mevan-Schwert"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:137
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The Mevan Sword is pure evil.  It surfaced early this century, after being buried under a pile of rubble since the Great Cataclysm.  It is not known who made it, or why, but most who have used it either swore by it or died by it. (Effects: Breaks after first use)"
msgid ""
"The Mevan Sword is pure evil.  It surfaced early this century, after being buried under a pile of rubble since the Great Cataclysm.  It is not known who made it, or why, but most who have used it either swore by it or died by it. (Effects: Breaks after its first attack)"
msgstr ""
"Das Mevan-Schwert ist durch und durch böse.  Es tauchte zu Beginn dieses Jahrhunderts wieder auf, nachdem es seit dem Großen Sturm der Elemente unter einem Haufen Schutt begraben lag.  Man weiß nicht, wer es geschmiedet hat oder warum, aber die meisten, die es benutzten, schworen entweder darauf oder starben dadurch. (Effekte: Zerbricht nach dem ersten Gebrauch)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:138
msgid "Jorhgamesh"
msgstr "Jorhgamesh"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:138
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Jorhgamesh was comissioned by Olaf the Fat during his short reign as Jarl of Frosgard.  He believed that with this sword he could conquer and unite all the Clans of Chedian (Effects: +10 to Speed, +20 to Accuracy, -50 to SP)"
msgid ""
"Jorhgamesh was commissioned by Olaf the Fat during his short reign as Jarl of Frosgard.  He believed that with this sword he could conquer and unite all the Clans of Chedian. (Effects: +40 Speed, +40 Accuracy, -50 SP)"
msgstr ""
"Jorhgamesh wurde von Olaf dem Dicken während seiner kurzen Herrschaft als Jarl von Frosgard in Auftrag gegeben.  Er glaubte, mit diesem Schwert alle Clans von Chedian erobern und vereinen zu können (Effekte: +10 Schnelligkeit, +20 Genauigkeit, -50 ZP)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:139
msgid "Black's Heart"
msgstr "Herz des Schwarzen"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:139
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Long ago, there was a group of Chedian warriors lead by a man named Halfred the Black.  This dagger was his constant companion.  After his death, the dagger was buried with him.  His grave however was soon looted, it's contents taken and sold. (Effects: Increased damage, Increased chance to hit, Increased speed)"
msgid ""
"Long ago, there was a group of Chedian warriors led by a man named Halfred the Black.  This dagger was his constant companion.  After his death, the dagger was buried with him.  His grave however was soon looted, its contents taken and sold. (Effects: +20 to hit, +10 damage, faster recovery)"
msgstr ""
"Vor langer Zeit gab es eine Schar chedianischer Krieger, angeführt von einem Mann namens Halfred der Schwarze.  Dieser Dolch war sein ständiger Begleiter.  Nach seinem Tod wurde der Dolch mit ihm begraben.  Sein Grab wurde jedoch bald geplündert, und sein Inhalt wurde fortgeschafft und verkauft. (Effekte: Erhöhter Schaden, erhöhte Trefferchance, erhöhte Schnelligkeit)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:14
msgid "Baselard"
msgstr "Basilard"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:14
msgid "This dagger is often worn by peasants."
msgstr "Diesen Dolch tragen oft Bauern."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:140
msgid "Integris"
msgstr "Integris"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:140
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Named after the Old Ursanian Emperor who commited suicide in 225 BC, this is the dagger that he used to finally end his life.  Emperor Integris was often called the \"Suicidal Emperor\" because of his many attempts to end his own life.  Ironically, on most of his attempts, the weapon broke in his hand before he could complete the task. (Effects: +15 pts of Poison damage; Reputed +35 to hit and damage)"
msgid ""
"Named after the Old Ursanian Emperor who committed suicide in 225 BC, this is the dagger that he used to finally end his life.  Emperor Integris was often called the \"Suicidal Emperor\" because of his many attempts to end his own life.  Ironically, on most of his attempts, the weapon broke in his hand before he could complete the task. (Effects: +20 to hit, +15 damage, +15 poison damage per hit)"
msgstr ""
"Benannt nach dem altursanischen Kaiser, der 225 v. K. Selbstmord beging, ist dies der Dolch, mit dem er seinem Leben schließlich ein Ende setzte.  Kaiser Integris wurde wegen seiner vielen Versuche, sich das Leben zu nehmen, oft der \"Lebensmüde Kaiser\" genannt.  Ironischerweise zerbrach die Waffe bei den meisten seiner Versuche in seiner Hand, bevor er sein Werk vollenden konnte. (Effekte: +15 Punkte Giftschaden; angeblich +35 auf Treffer und Schaden)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:141
msgid "Bloodaxe"
msgstr "Bloodaxe"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:141
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This axe is named after the Sturmford warrior Sven Bloodaxe who was ever victorious in combat.  Although it is denied by many, he finally died in 340 AC of old age. (Effects: +10 to all resistances; 40% chance to \"poison\" target at GM level.)"
msgid ""
"This axe is named after the Sturmford warrior Sven Bloodaxe who was ever victorious in combat.  Although it is denied by many, he finally died in 340 AC of old age. (Effects: +30 Endurance, +10 to all resistances, 40% chance to poison the target at Grandmaster)"
msgstr ""
"Diese Axt ist nach dem Krieger Sven Bloodaxe aus Sturmford benannt, der im Kampf stets siegreich war.  Auch wenn viele es bestreiten, starb er schließlich 340 n. K. an Altersschwäche. (Effekte: +10 auf alle Resistenzen; 40% Chance, das Ziel auf Großmeister-Stufe zu \"vergiften\".)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:142
msgid "Sygnir"
msgstr "Sygnir"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:142
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This axe was forged 200 BC in Minespring.  The dwarves of that era were exceptional at their ability to create incredible weapons.  In 73 AC, Ichvan I tried to convince the dwarves to begin making weapons for his new Mendossian Army.  After 2 years of negotiation, Ichvan tired of their refusals and razed Minespring. (Effects: Extra damage; +6 Armsmaster, +6 Blade skill; of Regeneration)"
msgid ""
"This axe was forged 200 BC in Minespring.  The dwarves of that era were exceptional at their ability to create incredible weapons.  In 73 AC, Ichvan I tried to convince the dwarves to begin making weapons for his new Mendossian Army.  After 2 years of negotiation, Ichvan tired of their refusals and razed Minespring. (Effects: +6 Axe, +6 Armsmaster, +10 damage per hit, regenerates HP)"
msgstr ""
"Diese Axt wurde 200 v. K. in Minespring geschmiedet.  Die Zwerge jener Zeit waren außergewöhnlich begabt darin, unglaubliche Waffen zu erschaffen.  Im Jahre 73 n. K. versuchte Ichvan I., die Zwerge zu überreden, Waffen für sein neues Mendossisches Heer herzustellen.  Nach 2 Jahren Verhandlungen hatte Ichvan ihre Weigerungen satt und machte Minespring dem Erdboden gleich. (Effekte: Zusätzlicher Schaden; +6 Waffenmeister, +6 Fertigkeit Klinge; der Regeneration)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:143
msgid "Everstrike"
msgstr "Everstrike"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:143
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Made of Elemental Thjorad, this weapon was one of the finest creations from the famed weaponsmith Borfinn Ironhands.  He always claimed he was not adept at making missle throwers, but this weapon is clearly the finest example of anything he ever made. (Effects: 100% accuracy)"
msgid ""
"Made of Elemental Thjorad, this weapon was one of the finest creations from the famed weaponsmith Borfinn Ironhands.  He always claimed he was not adept at making missile throwers, but this weapon is clearly the finest example of anything he ever made. (Effects: +5 Bow, faster recovery, always hits)"
msgstr ""
"Diese Waffe aus Elementar-Thjorad war eine der besten Schöpfungen des berühmten Waffenschmieds Borfinn Eisenhand.  Er behauptete stets, im Bau von Fernwaffen nicht geübt zu sein, doch diese Waffe ist eindeutig das beste Stück, das er je geschaffen hat. (Effekte: 100% Genauigkeit)"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:144
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This dagger was given to Aesir the Scholar as a reward in the Thronish town of Nirheim.  She spent most of her life travelling from town to town across Chedian healing children and teaching her skills to townsfolks.  A Merchant gave up his prized dagger as a gift for saving the life of his son. (Effects: +100 HP; Slow; 3 attacks)"
msgid ""
"This dagger was given to Aesir the Scholar as a reward in the Thronish town of Nirheim.  She spent most of her life travelling from town to town across Chedian healing children and teaching her skills to townsfolks.  A Merchant gave up his prized dagger as a gift for saving the life of his son. (Effects: +100 HP, slower recovery, three projectiles per throw)"
msgstr ""
"Dieser Dolch wurde Aesir der Gelehrten in der thronischen Stadt Nirheim als Belohnung geschenkt.  Sie verbrachte den größten Teil ihres Lebens damit, von Stadt zu Stadt durch Chedian zu reisen, Kinder zu heilen und den Leuten ihre Fertigkeiten beizubringen.  Ein Kaufmann gab seinen kostbarsten Dolch als Geschenk dafür her, daß sie seinem Sohn das Leben gerettet hatte. (Effekte: +100 TP; Langsam; 3 Angriffe)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:144
msgid "Trolleri"
msgstr "Trolleri"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:145
msgid "Tillhygge"
msgstr "Tillhygge"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:145
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Tillhygge was unearthed on the Isle of Ashes in 75 AC when a group of Scavengers were picking through the remains of Verhoffin's Tower.  When they returned to the mainland, they claimed it to be haunted by the ghost of Verhoffin himself and soon sold the axe. (Effects: +10 Might, +30 Accuracy; of Disease, of Mastery)"
msgid ""
"Tillhygge was unearthed on the Isle of Ashes in 75 AC when a group of Scavengers were picking through the remains of Verhoffin's Tower.  When they returned to the mainland, they claimed it to be haunted by the ghost of Verhoffin himself and soon sold the axe. (Effects: +10 Might, +30 Accuracy, +5 Repair Item, +5 disease damage per hit)"
msgstr ""
"Tillhygge wurde im Jahre 75 n. K. auf der Ascheninsel ausgegraben, als eine Gruppe von Plünderern die Überreste von Verhoffins Turm durchwühlte.  Als sie aufs Festland zurückkehrten, behaupteten sie, die Axt werde vom Geist Verhoffins selbst heimgesucht, und verkauften sie bald. (Effekte: +10 Stärke, +30 Genauigkeit; der Krankheit, der Meisterschaft)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:146
msgid "Kraftig Bage"
msgstr "Kraftig Bage"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:146
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This bow was carried into battle by the mighty warrior Halfnorr the Ox-Shouldered.  It conferred upon him great strength and skill.  He was slain by another warrior, Sven Bloodaxe, when they met in battle in Thjorgard. (Effects: +10 to all stats; +7 Bow)"
msgid ""
"This bow was carried into battle by the mighty warrior Halfnorr the Ox-Shouldered.  It conferred upon him great strength and skill.  He was slain by another warrior, Sven Bloodaxe, when they met in battle in Thjorgard. (Effects: +10 to all stats, +7 Bow)"
msgstr ""
"Dieser Bogen wurde vom mächtigen Krieger Halfnorr dem Ochsenschultrigen in die Schlacht getragen.  Er verlieh ihm große Kraft und großes Geschick.  Er wurde von einem anderen Krieger, Sven Bloodaxe, erschlagen, als sie in Thjorgard im Kampf aufeinandertrafen. (Effekte: +10 auf alle Attribute; +7 Bogen)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:147
msgid "Blackpowder"
msgstr "Schwarzpulver"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:147
msgid "Hand Cannon"
msgstr "Handkanone"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:147
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This device was created by the mad scholar Roj'ere sometime before his death in 320 AC.  He was called a genius by some, a madman by others.  This paticular invetion uses a strange black powder to propel a projectile from it's muzzle.  Roj'ere was extremely proud of this invention, but died before he could refine it and make it safer to use. (Effects: Bypass opponent's AC, Extra damage, Slow recovery, 2% Chance per use of breaking and causing damage to player.)"
msgid ""
"This device was created by the mad scholar Roj'ere sometime before his death in 320 AC.  He was called a genius by some, a madman by others.  This particular invention uses a strange black powder to propel a projectile from its muzzle.  Roj'ere was extremely proud of this invention, but died before he could refine it and make it safer to use. (Effects: +15 damage per hit, slower recovery, halves the target's AC, 2% chance per shot to break and hurt the wielder)"
msgstr ""
"Dieses Gerät wurde irgendwann vor seinem Tod im Jahre 320 n. K. vom verrückten Gelehrten Roj'ere erschaffen.  Manche nannten ihn ein Genie, andere einen Wahnsinnigen.  Diese besondere Erfindung verwendet ein seltsames schwarzes Pulver, um ein Geschoß aus ihrer Mündung zu treiben.  Roj'ere war äußerst stolz auf diese Erfindung, starb aber, bevor er sie verfeinern und sicherer machen konnte. (Effekte: Umgeht die RK des Gegners, zusätzlicher Schaden, langsame Erholung, bei jedem Gebrauch 2% Chance, zu zerbrechen und dem Charakter Schaden zuzufügen.)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:148
msgid "Gungnir"
msgstr "Gungnir"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:148
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Gungnir was fashioned by Hanndl himself to serve as his weapon during the Great Reckoning that is fated to happen one day.  On the day Krohn forsaw the coming of this day, he demanded all his gods arm themselves with weapons of great power.  Somehow, Hanndl's spear surfaced in Chedian (Effects: of puncturing (20% chance to bypass opponent's AC).  Extra Damage)"
msgid ""
"Gungnir was fashioned by Hanndl himself to serve as his weapon during the Great Reckoning that is fated to happen one day.  On the day Krohn foresaw the coming of this day, he demanded all his gods arm themselves with weapons of great power.  Somehow, Hanndl's spear surfaced in Chedian. (Effects: +15 damage per hit, 20% chance to ignore the target's AC)"
msgstr ""
"Gungnir wurde von Hanndl selbst geschaffen, um ihm in der Großen Abrechnung als Waffe zu dienen, die eines Tages kommen soll.  An dem Tag, an dem Krohn das Kommen dieses Tages vorhersah, verlangte er, daß sich alle seine Götter mit Waffen von großer Macht rüsten.  Irgendwie tauchte Hanndls Speer in Chedian auf (Effekte: des Durchbohrens (20% Chance, die RK des Gegners zu umgehen).  Zusätzlicher Schaden)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:149
msgid "Formanir"
msgstr "Formanir"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:149
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This spear was cast over the heads of the Tredskas rebels by Krohn himself when they rebelled against the gods and tried to capture Arslegard.  Desipte their leader being one of the most powerful magicians of the time, and the army made up of hundreds of thousands of skilled warriors, not a single Tredskas rebel left the battlefield that day.  Krohn left this spear behind as a warning to mortals who thought to rebel. (Effects: -10 to AC, +30 Might, -10 Endurance; Grandmaster's, of Permanance.)"
msgid ""
"This spear was cast over the heads of the Tredskas rebels by Krohn himself when they rebelled against the gods and tried to capture Arslegard.  Despite their leader being one of the most powerful magicians of the time, and the army made up of hundreds of thousands of skilled warriors, not a single Tredskas rebel left the battlefield that day.  Krohn left this spear behind as a warning to mortals who thought to rebel. (Effects: +50 Might, -10 Endurance, -10 AC, +5 Spear)"
msgstr ""
"Diesen Speer schleuderte Krohn selbst über die Köpfe der Tredskas-Rebellen, als sie sich gegen die Götter erhoben und versuchten, Arslegard einzunehmen.  Obwohl ihr Anführer einer der mächtigsten Magier seiner Zeit war und ihr Heer aus Hunderttausenden geübter Krieger bestand, verließ an jenem Tag kein einziger Tredskas-Rebell das Schlachtfeld.  Krohn ließ diesen Speer als Warnung an alle Sterblichen zurück, die an Rebellion dachten. (Effekte: -10 RK, +30 Stärke, -10 Ausdauer; des Großmeisters, der Beständigkeit.)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:15
msgid "Chedian Dirk"
msgstr "Chedianischer Dirk"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:15
msgid ""
"This dagger is the Chedian's constant companion.  Should he ever have to go somewhere without his sword, he would take this dagger with him."
msgstr ""
"Dieser Dolch ist der ständige Begleiter eines jeden Chedianers.  Sollte er jemals ohne sein Schwert irgendwohin gehen müssen, würde er diesen Dolch mitnehmen."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:150
msgid "Einherjar"
msgstr "Einherjar"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:150
msgid ""
"This halberd is said to carry with it the souls of men slain by it.  It has an unusual effect on those wielding it.  Its first owner was said to have gone mad.  It's second owner gave it away and threw himself from a cliff.  The tales of tragedy this halberd carries are long and sad. (Effects: +40 Might, Vampiric, 10% chance of insanity each week, 10% chance each week to lose a tenth of HP)"
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:151
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Literally Old Ursanian for \"Stick Cutter\" This is the only surviving example left.  It was used by the Ursanian Persana Garda, the men who were personally responsible for the Emperor's safety.  This weapon contributed in no small part to the fear the Persana Garda put in the hearts of men. (Effects: +30 Might, +10 Endurance; 5% chance to cast \"Enrage\" on target at GM level.)"
msgid ""
"Literally Old Ursanian for \"Stick Cutter\" This is the only surviving example left.  It was used by the Ursanian Persana Garda, the men who were personally responsible for the Emperor's safety.  This weapon contributed in no small part to the fear the Persana Garda put in the hearts of men. (Effects: +30 Might, +10 Endurance, 5% chance to enrage the target at Grandmaster)"
msgstr ""
"Wörtlich Altursanisch für \"Stockschneider\".  Dies ist das einzige erhaltene Exemplar.  Sie wurde von der Ursanischen Persana Garda benutzt, den Männern, die persönlich für die Sicherheit des Kaisers verantwortlich waren.  Diese Waffe trug nicht wenig dazu bei, daß die Persana Garda den Menschen Furcht ins Herz pflanzte. (Effekte: +30 Stärke, +10 Ausdauer; 5% Chance, auf Großmeister-Stufe \"Rasen\" auf das Ziel zu wirken.)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:151
msgid "Stouka Couta"
msgstr "Stouka Couta"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:152
msgid "Vanir's Hammer"
msgstr "Vanirs Hammer"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:152
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Vanir's Hammer was created by the legendary sorcerer Vanir several hundred years ago.  He was as adept at wielding this weapon as he was at sorcery.  Many people comment how this is not a hammer, but a cudgel, to which Vanir would reply \"But what is a hammer?  Does the name matter if it can crush skulls?\"  Not many on the receiving end of his hammer argued with him. (Effects: +30 Might, +10 Endurance; 5% Chance to cast \"Enrage\" on target at GM level.)"
msgid ""
"Vanir's Hammer was created by the legendary sorcerer Vanir several hundred years ago.  He was as adept at wielding this weapon as he was at sorcery.  Many people comment how this is not a hammer, but a cudgel, to which Vanir would reply \"But what is a hammer?  Does the name matter if it can crush skulls?\"  Not many on the receiving end of his hammer argued with him. (Effects: +30 Might, +10 Endurance, 5% chance to enrage the target at Grandmaster)"
msgstr ""
"Vanirs Hammer wurde vor mehreren hundert Jahren von dem legendären Zauberer Vanir geschaffen. Er führte diese Waffe ebenso geschickt, wie er die Zauberei beherrschte. Viele merken an, daß dies kein Hammer, sondern ein Knüppel sei, worauf Vanir zu erwidern pflegte: \"Aber was ist schon ein Hammer? Spielt der Name eine Rolle, wenn er Schädel zertrümmern kann?\" Nicht viele von denen, die seinen Hammer zu spüren bekamen, widersprachen ihm. (Effekte: +30 Stärke, +10 Ausdauer; 5% Chance, auf Großmeister-Stufe \"Raserei\" auf das Ziel zu wirken.)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:153
msgid "Blutterbunger"
msgstr "Blutterbunger"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:153
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Blutterbunger was a popular weapon in 480 AC when it was discovered.  It has the ability to confound an opponent, making it extremly popular in barroom brawls as well as on the battlefield.  It was owned by Fyri the Goat-Face until, in a barfight, he somehow managed to hit himself with it and knocked himself unconscious. (Effects: of Bruisers; 5% chance of stunning opponent.  If fail vs skill 70% chance knocking self unconscious.)"
msgid ""
"Blutterbunger was a popular weapon in 480 AC when it was discovered.  It has the ability to confound an opponent, making it extremely popular in barroom brawls as well as on the battlefield.  It was owned by Fyri the Goat-Face until, in a barfight, he somehow managed to hit himself with it and knocked himself unconscious. (Effects: +40 Might, +20 Endurance, +5 Mace, 5% chance to stun the target, 70% chance to knock the wielder unconscious when a hit does not stun)"
msgstr ""
"Blutterbunger war eine beliebte Waffe, als sie im Jahre 480 nach der Großen Katastrophe entdeckt wurde. Sie vermag einen Gegner zu verwirren, was sie bei Wirtshausschlägereien ebenso beliebt machte wie auf dem Schlachtfeld. Sie gehörte Fyri Ziegengesicht, bis er sich bei einer Kneipenschlägerei irgendwie selbst damit traf und sich bewußtlos schlug. (Effekte: der Raufbolde; 5% Chance, den Gegner zu betäuben. Bei Fehlschlag gegen die Fertigkeit 70% Chance, sich selbst bewußtlos zu schlagen.)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:154
msgid "Manarus"
msgstr "Manarus"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:154
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This morning star is named after the mythical hero Manarus who became the guiding star in the northern sky.  The history of this weapon is not known, but it is said to bestow great skill on magic users. (Effects: +80 SP; The Grandmaster's, of the Jajarb)"
msgid ""
"This morning star is named after the mythical hero Manarus who became the guiding star in the northern sky.  The history of this weapon is not known, but it is said to bestow great skill on magic users. (Effects: +30 Intellect, +30 Personality, +80 SP, +5 Mace)"
msgstr ""
"Dieser Morgenstern ist nach dem mythischen Helden Manarus benannt, der zum Leitstern am nördlichen Himmel wurde. Die Geschichte dieser Waffe ist unbekannt, doch es heißt, sie verleihe Magiekundigen großes Geschick. (Effekte: +80 ZP; des Großmeisters, des Jajarb)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:155
msgid "Samarjit"
msgstr "Samarjit"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:155
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This staff is made of an unknown metal.  It is surprisingly light, and also very, very old.  It was found with documents written in Old Ursanian that suggest it predates even the earliest mention of the Ursanian Empire.  Not even the documents explain who made it, how they made it, or where it came from. (Effects: +80 Might, +20 Endurance, -20 Speed; of Permanance, Master's)"
msgid ""
"This staff is made of an unknown metal.  It is surprisingly light, and also very, very old.  It was found with documents written in Old Ursanian that suggest it predates even the earliest mention of the Ursanian Empire.  Not even the documents explain who made it, how they made it, or where it came from. (Effects: +80 Might, +20 Endurance, -20 Speed, +3 Staff)"
msgstr ""
"Dieser Stab besteht aus einem unbekannten Metall. Er ist überraschend leicht und zudem sehr, sehr alt. Man fand ihn zusammen mit Schriften in Altursanisch, die nahelegen, daß er sogar älter ist als die früheste Erwähnung des Ursanischen Reiches. Nicht einmal die Schriften verraten, wer ihn geschaffen hat, wie er gefertigt wurde oder woher er stammt. (Effekte: +80 Stärke, +20 Ausdauer, -20 Schnelligkeit; der Beständigkeit, des Meisters)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:156
msgid "Maul"
msgstr "Schlägel"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:156
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This maul first appeared about 10 years AC, when most people were still picking up the pieces of the Great Cataclysm.  It is said to be made out of pure Elemental Thjorad, and is very, very heavy.  Many smiths have tried to copy this maul, and have only suceeded in making very heavy magic items. (Effects: 5-15 pts of Elemental Damage.  10% Chance of killing target.)"
msgid ""
"This maul first appeared about 10 years AC, when most people were still picking up the pieces of the Great Cataclysm.  It is said to be made out of pure Elemental Thjorad, and is very, very heavy.  Many smiths have tried to copy this maul, and have only succeeded in making very heavy magic items. (Effects: +10 damage per hit, 10% chance to kill the target outright)"
msgstr ""
"Dieser Schlägel tauchte erstmals etwa 10 Jahre nach der Großen Katastrophe auf, als die meisten Menschen noch dabei waren, die Trümmer aufzulesen. Es heißt, er sei aus reinem Elementar-Thjorad gefertigt, und er ist sehr, sehr schwer. Viele Schmiede haben versucht, diesen Schlägel nachzuahmen, doch es ist ihnen nur gelungen, sehr schwere magische Gegenstände herzustellen. (Effekte: 5-15 Punkte Elementarschaden. 10% Chance, das Ziel zu töten.)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:157
msgid "Spencer's Obedience"
msgstr "Spencers Gehorsam"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:157
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This is the club that General Spencer used to keep his troops in line.  He often found them playing card games intstead of staying at their posts, so he had this magical club created to \"inspire\" them to do their jobs.  It proved to be very effective. (Effects: +10 to Speed; of the Reel)"
msgid ""
"This is the club that General Spencer used to keep his troops in line.  He often found them playing card games instead of staying at their posts, so he had this magical club created to \"inspire\" them to do their jobs.  It proved to be very effective. (Effects: +20 Might, +30 Speed, stuns the target on every hit)"
msgstr ""
"Dies ist die Keule, mit der General Spencer seine Truppen bei der Stange hielt. Oft ertappte er sie beim Kartenspiel, statt daß sie auf ihren Posten blieben, und so ließ er diese magische Keule anfertigen, um sie zur Erfüllung ihrer Pflichten zu \"ermutigen\". Sie erwies sich als sehr wirkungsvoll. (Effekte: +10 Schnelligkeit; des Taumelns)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:158
msgid "Mjulnir"
msgstr "Mjulnir"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:158
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Mjulnir is often called \"The Hammer of the Gods\" and for good reason.  It is said that the god Krohn lost it when he hurled it at his wife after a quarrel.  It is a massive weapon, meant to be wielded by a massive warrior.  It is also rumored that Krohn has vowed to reclaim his weapon, and destroy the man who has kept it from him. (Effects: -20 Speed; 16-25 pts of Elemental Damage.  Divine Intervention will always fail.)"
msgid ""
"Mjulnir is often called \"The Hammer of the Gods\" and for good reason.  It is said that the god Krohn lost it when he hurled it at his wife after a quarrel.  It is a massive weapon, meant to be wielded by a massive warrior.  It is also rumored that Krohn has vowed to reclaim his weapon, and destroy the man who has kept it from him. (Effects: +50 Might, -20 Speed, +20 damage per hit, Divine Intervention always fails)"
msgstr ""
"Mjulnir wird oft \"Der Hammer der Götter\" genannt, und das aus gutem Grund. Es heißt, der Gott Krohn habe ihn verloren, als er ihn nach einem Streit nach seiner Frau schleuderte. Es ist eine gewaltige Waffe, geschaffen für einen gewaltigen Krieger. Man munkelt auch, Krohn habe geschworen, seine Waffe zurückzuholen und den Mann zu vernichten, der sie ihm vorenthalten hat. (Effekte: -20 Schnelligkeit; 16-25 Punkte Elementarschaden. Gottes Eingriff schlägt immer fehl.)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:159
msgid "Igdrasine"
msgstr "Igdrasine"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:159
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Legend has it this armor was a gift from Igrassa herself to Dagna Kramartrag, for his service to her temple. (Effects: +10 to Magic)"
msgid ""
"Legend has it this armor was a gift from Igrassa herself to Dagna Kramartrag, for his service to her temple. (Effects: +30 Intellect, +30 Personality)"
msgstr ""
"Der Legende nach war diese Rüstung ein Geschenk von Igrassa selbst an Dagna Kramartrag für seine Dienste an ihrem Tempel. (Effekte: +10 Magie)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:16
msgid ""
"This dagger is weighted and balanced for throwing.  Like the other throwing weapons found in Chedian, it is magically enchanted to return."
msgstr ""
"Dieser Dolch ist zum Werfen gewichtet und ausbalanciert. Wie die anderen Wurfwaffen in Chedian ist er magisch verzaubert, so daß er zurückkehrt."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:144 assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:16
msgid "Throwing Dagger"
msgstr "Wurfdolch"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:160
msgid "Poltergeist"
msgstr "Poltergeist"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:160
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This armor was allegedly made from the chains some ghosts carry with them.  Whether it is true or not, it certainly has some ghostly properties.  It weighs nearly nothing at all, and carries with it a foreboding cloud.  It also seems to make the same sound as the poor souls who are chained to the place of their death. (Effects: of Regeneration; 10% chance of opponent becoming afraid.)"
msgid ""
"This armor was allegedly made from the chains some ghosts carry with them.  Whether it is true or not, it certainly has some ghostly properties.  It weighs nearly nothing at all, and carries with it a foreboding cloud.  It also seems to make the same sound as the poor souls who are chained to the place of their death. (Effects: +30 Speed, regenerates HP, 10% chance to frighten the target on a hit)"
msgstr ""
"Diese Rüstung soll aus den Ketten gefertigt worden sein, die manche Geister mit sich tragen. Ob das stimmt oder nicht, sie hat jedenfalls einige geisterhafte Eigenschaften. Sie wiegt so gut wie nichts und ist von einer unheilvollen Wolke umgeben. Zudem scheint sie dieselben Geräusche von sich zu geben wie die armen Seelen, die an den Ort ihres Todes gekettet sind. (Effekte: der Regeneration; 10% Chance, daß der Gegner verängstigt wird.)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:161
msgid "Swordsbane"
msgstr "Schwertbann"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:161
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This armor was worn by Leit the Crusader during his reign as leader of the Thronheim Clan.  It was with this armor he slayed the foul creatures that inhabited the area that would become Thronheim City.  It is said to prevent sword from ever touching skin. (Effects: +40 AC vs melee attacks, -10 AC vs ranged attacks)"
msgid ""
"This armor was worn by Leit the Crusader during his reign as leader of the Thronheim Clan.  It was with this armor he slayed the foul creatures that inhabited the area that would become Thronheim City.  It is said to prevent sword from ever touching skin. (Effects: +40 AC against melee attacks, -10 AC against missiles)"
msgstr ""
"Diese Rüstung trug Leit der Kreuzritter während seiner Herrschaft als Anführer des Thronheim-Clans. In dieser Rüstung erschlug er die widerwärtigen Kreaturen, die das Gebiet bewohnten, aus dem später die Stadt Thronheim werden sollte. Es heißt, sie verhindere, daß jemals ein Schwert die Haut berührt. (Effekte: +40 RK gegen Nahkampfangriffe, -10 RK gegen Fernkampfangriffe)"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:162
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "It is said that this helm is made from the skull of Ilthic, the most powerful witch of the Ursanian Empire. Rumor is, Emperor Ralfor himself severed her head.  After removing the unnecessary parts, he had the new helmet enchanted against magical attacks. (Effects: +20 all resistances, +20 AC vs magic attacks)"
msgid ""
"It is said that this helm is made from the skull of Ilthic, the most powerful witch of the Ursanian Empire. Rumor is, Emperor Ralfor himself severed her head.  After removing the unnecessary parts, he had the new helmet enchanted against magical attacks. (Effects: +20 to all resistances, +20 AC against magic)"
msgstr ""
"Es heißt, dieser Helm sei aus dem Schädel von Ilthic gefertigt, der mächtigsten Hexe des Ursanischen Reiches. Gerüchten zufolge hat Kaiser Ralfor ihr eigenhändig den Kopf abgeschlagen. Nachdem er die überflüssigen Teile entfernt hatte, ließ er den neuen Helm gegen magische Angriffe verzaubern. (Effekte: +20 auf alle Resistenzen, +20 RK gegen magische Angriffe)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:162
msgid "Witchbane"
msgstr "Hexenbann"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:163
msgid "Brongnoker"
msgstr "Brongnoker"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:163
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Pitted and dented, this helm does not look like much.  Looks can be deceiving however.  Brongnoker was made before the founding of the Ursanian Empire, with long lost forging techniques.  This helm is probably the finest protection for the head in the world. (Effects: +10 all stats, +10 Armor skill)"
msgid ""
"Pitted and dented, this helm does not look like much.  Looks can be deceiving however.  Brongnoker was made before the founding of the Ursanian Empire, with long lost forging techniques.  This helm is probably the finest protection for the head in the world. (Effects: +10 to all stats, +10 to the armor skills)"
msgstr ""
"Zerkratzt und verbeult, macht dieser Helm nicht viel her. Doch der Schein kann trügen. Brongnoker wurde vor der Gründung des Ursanischen Reiches mit längst vergessenen Schmiedekünsten gefertigt. Dieser Helm ist wohl der beste Kopfschutz der Welt. (Effekte: +10 auf alle Attribute, +10 Fertigkeit Rüstung)"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:164
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "These boots were made for walking.  However, because of the special enchantments put upon them to protect the traveller's feet, they have been used more often by the fortunate soldier who happened upon them. (Effects: +10 Speed; of Everlasting, of Regeneration, of Amelieoration; +10 to all resistances)"
msgid ""
"These boots were made for walking.  However, because of the special enchantments put upon them to protect the traveller's feet, they have been used more often by the fortunate soldier who happened upon them. (Effects: +10 Speed, +10 to all resistances, regenerates HP, immune to weakness and drunkenness, never breaks)"
msgstr ""
"Diese Stiefel wurden zum Wandern gemacht. Wegen der besonderen Verzauberungen, die die Füße des Reisenden schützen sollen, wurden sie jedoch meist von dem glücklichen Soldaten getragen, der zufällig auf sie stieß. (Effekte: +10 Schnelligkeit; der Ewigkeit, der Regeneration, der Linderung; +10 auf alle Resistenzen)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:165
msgid "Laet'ax"
msgstr "Laet'ax"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:165
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This pair of soft leather gloves was found outside Verhoffin's tower in 300 AC.  They are soft, and somewhat slippery.  No matter the size of the wearer's hand, they seem to always fit. (Effects: -10 Accuracy, +10 Luck; +5 Disarm Trap)"
msgid ""
"This pair of soft leather gloves was found outside Verhoffin's tower in 300 AC.  They are soft, and somewhat slippery.  No matter the size of the wearer's hand, they seem to always fit. (Effects: -20 Accuracy, +40 Luck, +10 Disarm Traps)"
msgstr ""
"Dieses Paar weicher Lederhandschuhe wurde im Jahre 300 nach der Großen Katastrophe vor Verhoffins Turm gefunden. Sie sind weich und etwas rutschig. Ganz gleich, wie groß die Hand des Trägers ist, sie scheinen immer zu passen. (Effekte: -10 Genauigkeit, +10 Glück; +5 Fallen entschärfen)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:166
msgid "Arrowfoe"
msgstr "Pfeilfeind"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:166
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This sheild was carried by the mighty warrior Hrothgar Krohnssen.  He claimed to be the son of Krohn himself, and possesed mighty strength.  When a witch told him he was to be killed by an arrow, he had this shield constructed to protect him from that fate.  Unfortunately, the arrow that killed him struck him from behind. (Effects: +30 AC vs Missle weapons)"
msgid ""
"This shield was carried by the mighty warrior Hrothgar Krohnssen.  He claimed to be the son of Krohn himself, and possessed mighty strength.  When a witch told him he was to be killed by an arrow, he had this shield constructed to protect him from that fate.  Unfortunately, the arrow that killed him struck him from behind. (Effects: +30 Endurance, +30 AC against missiles)"
msgstr ""
"Diesen Schild trug der mächtige Krieger Hrothgar Krohnssen. Er behauptete, der Sohn Krohns selbst zu sein, und besaß gewaltige Kraft. Als eine Hexe ihm weissagte, er werde durch einen Pfeil sterben, ließ er diesen Schild anfertigen, um sich vor diesem Schicksal zu schützen. Leider traf ihn der tödliche Pfeil von hinten. (Effekte: +30 RK gegen Geschosse)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:167
msgid "Hubris"
msgstr "Hubris"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:167
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This belt was looted from the Chasm of the Dead, and is allegedly the belt that was worn by Emperor Hubris himself when he began to forge the Ursanian Empire.  Some scholars believe that this belt helped him defeat the invaders and create an empire. (Effects: +30 Might; +20 AC; of Endurance, of Protection, of Arms Mastery; Increased chance to hit target.)"
msgid ""
"This belt was looted from the Chasm of the Dead, and is allegedly the belt that was worn by Emperor Hubris himself when he began to forge the Ursanian Empire.  Some scholars believe that this belt helped him defeat the invaders and create an empire. (Effects: +30 Might, +10 Endurance, +20 AC, +5 Armsmaster)"
msgstr ""
"Dieser Gürtel wurde aus der Schlucht der Toten geraubt und soll der Gürtel sein, den Kaiser Hubris selbst trug, als er das Ursanische Reich zu schmieden begann. Manche Gelehrte glauben, daß dieser Gürtel ihm half, die Eindringlinge zu besiegen und ein Reich zu gründen. (Effekte: +30 Stärke; +20 RK; der Ausdauer, des Schutzes, der Waffenmeisterschaft; erhöhte Trefferchance.)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:168
msgid "Weregild"
msgstr "Wergeld"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:168
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Weregild was created by Snorri the Dwarf as a wedding gift for his soon to be son-in-law.  Unfortunately, another of his daughter's suitor's became jealous and stole the ring on the wedding night.  In his rage, he cursed the ring, and gave it back to the newlyweds.  Seeing through his deception, Snorri slew the suitor and cast the ring away. (Effects: +1000 gold per week.  Reputed -40 party Endurance.)"
msgid ""
"Weregild was created by Snorri the Dwarf as a wedding gift for his soon to be son-in-law.  Unfortunately, another of his daughter's suitors became jealous and stole the ring on the wedding night.  In his rage, he cursed the ring, and gave it back to the newlyweds.  Seeing through his deception, Snorri slew the suitor and cast the ring away. (Effects: +30 Luck, 1,000 gold each week, -40 Endurance for the whole party)"
msgstr ""
"Wergeld wurde von Snorri dem Zwerg als Hochzeitsgeschenk für seinen künftigen Schwiegersohn geschaffen. Leider wurde ein anderer Verehrer seiner Tochter eifersüchtig und stahl den Ring in der Hochzeitsnacht. In seiner Wut verfluchte er den Ring und gab ihn den Frischvermählten zurück. Snorri durchschaute die Täuschung, erschlug den Verehrer und warf den Ring fort. (Effekte: +1000 Gold pro Woche. Angeblich -40 Ausdauer der Gruppe.)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:169
msgid "Soulband"
msgstr "Seelenband"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:169
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Soulband wasn't so much created as it was evolved from something else.  It started it's life as a trinket worn by a small child who became possessed by a Revenant.  Since that time it has passed from owner to owner, taking a little piece of them with when it passed to it's new owner. (Effects: +50 SP; +5 Light, +3 Meditiation; of Speed)"
msgid ""
"Soulband wasn't so much created as it was evolved from something else.  It started its life as a trinket worn by a small child who became possessed by a Revenant.  Since that time it has passed from owner to owner, taking a little piece of them with it when it passed to its new owner. (Effects: +10 Speed, +50 SP, +5 Light Magic, +3 Meditation, faster recovery)"
msgstr ""
"Seelenband wurde nicht so sehr geschaffen, vielmehr entwickelte es sich aus etwas anderem. Es begann sein Dasein als Schmuckstück eines kleinen Kindes, das von einem Wiedergänger besessen wurde. Seitdem ist es von Besitzer zu Besitzer gewandert und hat jedem ein kleines Stück von ihm genommen, wenn es an seinen neuen Besitzer überging. (Effekte: +50 ZP; +5 Licht, +3 Meditation; der Schnelligkeit)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:17
msgid "Hatchet"
msgstr "Beil"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:17
msgid ""
"More a tool than a weapon, when necessary, one could make do with this axe"
msgstr ""
"Eher ein Werkzeug als eine Waffe; im Notfall könnte man sich jedoch mit dieser Axt behelfen."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:170
msgid "Sturkabygel"
msgstr "Sturkabygel"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:170
msgid ""
"Sturkabygel was looted from the dwarven town of Minespring when it was razed by Ichvan I in 75 AC.  It was taken by one of his soldiers who went on to become one of his most prominent generals.  After his death, it was kept in the family as an heirloom.  It was taken from them by the Thjoradric Raiders during a raid of Heronport. (Effects: +10 Might, +5 Endurance, +100 HP)"
msgstr ""
"Sturkabygel wurde aus der Zwergenstadt Minespring geraubt, als Ichvan I. sie im Jahre 75 nach der Großen Katastrophe dem Erdboden gleichmachte. Einer seiner Soldaten nahm die Waffe an sich und wurde später einer seiner bedeutendsten Generäle. Nach dessen Tod wurde sie als Erbstück in der Familie bewahrt. Bei einem Überfall auf Heronport wurde sie ihnen von den Thjoradric-Plünderern geraubt. (Effekte: +10 Stärke, +5 Ausdauer, +100 TP)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:171
msgid "Lubricious"
msgstr "Schlüpfrig"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:171
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Some claim that Lubricious was actually made from these ingredients: the slip of a snake, the sly of a fox, and the nimbleness of a hare.  It was given to Helga Gunnarsdotir by a salacious suitor.  Not caring a whit for him, she promptly sold the ring. (Effects: +20 AC; +5 Dodging; Reputed -3% to Damage.)"
msgid ""
"Some claim that Lubricious was actually made from these ingredients: the slip of a snake, the sly of a fox, and the nimbleness of a hare.  It was given to Helga Gunnarsdotir by a salacious suitor.  Not caring a whit for him, she promptly sold the ring. (Effects: +20 AC, +5 Dodging, 3% less physical damage taken)"
msgstr ""
"Manche behaupten, Schlüpfrig sei tatsächlich aus diesen Zutaten gefertigt worden: der Glätte einer Schlange, der List eines Fuchses und der Flinkheit eines Hasen. Ein lüsterner Verehrer schenkte ihn Helga Gunnarsdotir. Da sie sich nicht das Geringste aus ihm machte, verkaufte sie den Ring prompt. (Effekte: +20 RK; +5 Ausweichen; angeblich -3% Schaden.)"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:172
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This amulet was a gift from The Green Man.  Very few are blessed with a visit to The Green Man, and fewer still have a gift bestowed upon them for it. (Effects: +20 SP; +3 Meditation, +5 Light, +5 Spirit; of Regeneration)"
msgid ""
"This amulet was a gift from The Green Man.  Very few are blessed with a visit to The Green Man, and fewer still have a gift bestowed upon them for it. (Effects: +20 SP, +3 Meditation, +5 Light Magic, +5 Spirit Magic, regenerates HP)"
msgstr ""
"Dieses Amulett war ein Geschenk des Grünen Mannes. Nur sehr wenigen ist ein Besuch des Grünen Mannes vergönnt, und noch weniger erhalten dabei ein Geschenk. (Effekte: +20 ZP; +3 Meditation, +5 Licht, +5 Seele; der Regeneration)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:173
msgid "Mountbatten"
msgstr "Mountbatten"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:173
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This amulet was carried by the four mystical sages, Dirk, Stig, Nasty, and Barry.  These four men had, for a time carried a message of peace and happiness to the Chedian, before they were chased out forever.  In their hurry to go, they left this behind. (Effects: +5 Dark, +3 Perception; of Amelioration)"
msgid ""
"This amulet was carried by the four mystical sages, Dirk, Stig, Nasty, and Barry.  These four men had, for a time carried a message of peace and happiness to the Chedian, before they were chased out forever.  In their hurry to go, they left this behind. (Effects: +30 Personality, +5 Dark Magic, +3 Perception, immune to weakness and drunkenness)"
msgstr ""
"Dieses Amulett trugen die vier mystischen Weisen Dirk, Stig, Nasty und Barry. Diese vier Männer brachten den Chedianern eine Zeitlang eine Botschaft von Frieden und Glück, bevor sie für immer vertrieben wurden. In ihrer Eile ließen sie dies zurück. (Effekte: +5 Dunkel, +3 Wahrnehmung; der Linderung)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:174
msgid "Pendant of the Spheres"
msgstr "Anhänger der Sphären"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:174
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This pendant was taken by Nazrim the Assassin from Verhoffin's Tower around 10 BC.  Nazrim had been charged with slaying Verhoffin for his insolence towards the Ursanian Empire.  Many think that it is that event, the attempted assassination of Verhoffin that caused the Great Cataclysm. (Effects: +5 All magic skills, +3 Learning, +3 Meditation)"
msgid ""
"This pendant was taken by Nazrim the Assassin from Verhoffin's Tower around 10 BC.  Nazrim had been charged with slaying Verhoffin for his insolence towards the Ursanian Empire.  Many think that it is that event, the attempted assassination of Verhoffin that caused the Great Cataclysm. (Effects: +3 to all magic skills, +3 Learning, +3 Meditation)"
msgstr ""
"Diesen Anhänger nahm Nazrim der Meuchelmörder um das Jahr 10 vor der Großen Katastrophe aus Verhoffins Turm mit. Nazrim war beauftragt worden, Verhoffin für seine Unverschämtheit gegenüber dem Ursanischen Reich zu töten. Viele glauben, daß dieses Ereignis, der Mordanschlag auf Verhoffin, die Große Katastrophe auslöste. (Effekte: +5 auf alle Magiefertigkeiten, +3 Lernen, +3 Meditation)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:175
msgid "Fizbin of Misfortune"
msgstr "Fizbin des Unglücks"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:175
msgid "Holy Relic"
msgstr "Heilige Reliquie"

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:175
msgid ""
"The Fizbin always seems to appear in the worst of times.  Just when someone thinks things can't get any worse, they acquire the Fizbin.  It's fame precedes it, and most owners have a hard time getting rid of it. (Effects: While carried, for the whole party: +15 Might, +15 Accuracy, -20 Luck, +10 to all resistances, random encounters 15% more likely)"
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/mm9/data_tables/items.txt:176
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Beggers are often seen in the major towns of Chedian, and many complain to have any sort of adverse condition.  Oftentimes, a healer would curse the begger with the affliction he claimed to have.  One begger, Haelik the Diseased, created this amulet to protect himself from such healers. (Effects: -3 Learning; Immune to all conditions.  Drains Experience Points.)"
msgid ""
"Beggars are often seen in the major towns of Chedian, and many complain to have any sort of adverse condition.  Oftentimes, a healer would curse the beggar with the affliction he claimed to have.  One beggar, Haelik the Diseased, created this amulet to protect himself from such healers. (Effects: -3 Learning, immune to all conditions, 15% less experience)"
msgstr ""
"In den größeren Städten Chedians sieht man oft Bettler, und viele behaupten, an allerlei Gebrechen zu leiden. Nicht selten verfluchte ein Heiler einen Bettler mit genau dem Leiden, das dieser vorgab zu haben. Ein Bettler, Haelik der Kranke, schuf dieses Amulett, um sich vor solchen Heilern zu schützen. (Effekte: -3 Lernen; immun gegen alle Zustände. Entzieht Erfahrungspunkte.)"

